text:
GENERATE BURST NB-1 — Run C-9 test T8 (Matt R-C9-69): a NEW character made for the 3D test, a NORSE BARBARIAN: his BASE BODY as a CHARACTER SHEET for a 3D model. task_id "NB-1".

WHY this sheet exists (so you can judge your own result): a 3D model will be built from these four views, then rigged and animated. His armour, fur, helmet and weapons will be added LATER as separate pieces on top of this body. So this sheet shows him with the LEAST clothing and gear, and the four views must agree exactly, as four views of ONE body.

IMAGE 1 is a STYLE reference ONLY. Copy its HAND: the warm dark-brown ink line that varies in weight, the transparent watercolor washes that pool, granulate and bloom, the fine hatching in the shadows, the cream paper highlights, the warm moderate colour. Copy NOTHING else from it: not its character, face, hair, hood, robe, staff, bag, pose or clothing colours.

THE CHARACTER, a Norse barbarian, base body:
- a tall, powerfully built man of about thirty-five: broad shoulders and chest, heavy strong arms; a warrior's body, NOT a bodybuilder's; natural proportions, about seven and a half heads tall;
- BARE-CHESTED and bare-armed: weathered, lightly freckled skin, a few pale old scars on the chest and forearms; ONE band of dark blue-grey knotwork tattoo around his RIGHT upper arm only (his left arm is bare);
- RED-GOLD hair, cropped short at the sides of the head, the rest pulled back and bound into ONE thick braid that hangs straight down his back to between the shoulder blades; a full red-gold beard gathered at the chin into ONE short braid bound with a small bronze ring;
- loose wool TROUSERS in faded woad blue, gathered below the knee; pale linen LEG WRAPS wound from the ankle to just below the knee;
- plain brown leather ankle SHOES with clear toes;
- a plain brown leather BELT with a small bronze buckle; nothing hangs from it;
- NOTHING ELSE: no cloak, no fur, no tunic, no armour, no helmet, no bracers, no jewellery except the beard ring, no weapon, no shield, no bag, no pouch;
- a calm, level face: mouth closed, eyes open, looking straight ahead.

SHEET: ONE 1024x1536 PORTRAIT sheet on flat pure #00ff00 in a 2x2 grid: the SAME man in four views at the SAME scale, each view centred in its quarter, soles on one ground line per row, each figure filling most of its quarter's height. Top-left FRONT (facing the viewer); top-right his RIGHT SIDE (in profile, facing the viewer's right); bottom-left BACK (seen from behind); bottom-right his LEFT SIDE (in profile, facing the viewer's left).
POSE (for building and rigging a 3D model): a relaxed A-POSE. Both arms straight and held AWAY from the body at about 30 degrees, so that in the front and back views a clear gap of green shows between each arm and the torso. Hands OPEN: fingers together and straight, thumbs slightly apart, palms facing the thighs. Legs straight, feet a little apart and pointing forward, weight even. Head level, facing the same way as the body. The braid hangs straight down his back, clear of the arms. Nothing overlaps anything.
He must be ONE consistent man in all four views: the same face, hair, braid, beard, tattoo (on the RIGHT arm in every view where that arm shows), trousers, wraps, shoes and belt.
STYLE: the REGISTER CARD above governs line, washes, light and plate. Its manuscript-subject clause does not apply to this figure: his subject and costume are set by this brief (Matt R-C9-69). Paint him in IMAGE 1's hand. Soft even light; no cast shadows, no ground, no text, no labels, no cell borders, no other figures.

Two image_gen calls: variants a and b. ONE retry per variant only if a view is missing or has the wrong facing, the man differs between views, an arm touches the torso in the front or back view, any armour, fur, cloak, weapon or other gear appears, the tattoo is on the wrong arm, or the background is not flat green — name the reason. Copy outputs to out/NB-1_a.png and out/NB-1_b.png with sha256. No code. No other files. No web.
RETURN: receipt task_id "NB-1"; images = the files with prompt, references (role + path) and elapsed_s; calls_used = the TRUE number of image_gen calls; status; concerns. Never PASS/FAIL.
